  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires 24h reporting for confirmed incidents but omits investigation-stage reporting (acceptable). S2 sets a permanent 7% failure cap with no automatic ban for >5%, and S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 24 months and retrofit to 6 years with a feasibility escape, both favoring Northwind. S4 mandates built-in suppression at 36 months (acceptable), while S5 replaces mandatory recall with a discretionary review at 8/100k, both favoring Halcyon."
